-- An imported rule that reads a section GIVEN, as each operand of each
-- built-in connective (UNKNOWN-EVALUATION-SPEC §8 step 2).
--
-- `rate is high` and `rate is low` come from
-- ok/section-given-import-connective-def.l4, where `the rate` is 5 by default,
-- so the first is TRUE and the second FALSE. Named here, each is a closure
-- that has to be applied to that module's own cell before it is a BOOLEAN. A
-- connective must apply it, on either side, whether it is called by name or
-- through a parameter; handing the closure on unapplied would make the right
-- operand of a TRUE AND the closure itself, which no assertion below accepts.

IMPORT `section-given-import-connective-def`

GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM BOOLEAN AND BOOLEAN TO BOOLEAN
      p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
combine f p q MEANS f p q

GIVEN g IS A FUNCTION FROM BOOLEAN TO BOOLEAN
      p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
apply g p MEANS g p

-- Called by name.
#ASSERT `rate is high` AND TRUE
#ASSERT TRUE AND `rate is high`
#ASSERT NOT (`rate is low` OR FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (FALSE OR `rate is low`)
#ASSERT `rate is low` IMPLIES FALSE
#ASSERT TRUE IMPLIES `rate is high`
#ASSERT NOT `rate is low`

-- Through a parameter.
#ASSERT combine `__AND__` `rate is high` TRUE
#ASSERT combine `__AND__` TRUE `rate is high`
#ASSERT NOT (combine `__OR__` `rate is low` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (combine `__OR__` FALSE `rate is low`)
#ASSERT combine `__IMPLIES__` `rate is low` FALSE
#ASSERT combine `__IMPLIES__` TRUE `rate is high`
#ASSERT apply `__NOT__` `rate is low`
